# Tailwind v4 `@apply` — custom project classes

Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`) **rejects `@apply` of project component classes**, even when defined in imported CSS (`app-text-styles.css`, `app-text-colors.css`, dashboard `dash-*`). Dev/build fails with:

`Cannot apply unknown utility class 'dash-…'` or `'app-text-…'`

## Forbidden in `@apply`

| Prefix / class | Source |
|---|---|
| `dash-*` | Dashboard component classes |
| `app-*` | Figma typography (`app-text-*`, `app-header-*`, `app-button-*`) |
| `text-average`, `text-action`, `text-hint`, `text-title`, `text-neutral-000`, `text-secondary-300` | Semantic colors from `app-text-colors.css` |

## Rules

1. **Never** put custom project classes inside `@apply`:
   - Bad: `@apply flex dash-text-sm-sb;`
   - Bad: `@apply app-text-p1-regular text-average;`
   - Good: `@apply flex text-sm font-semibold;`

2. **`@apply` may only use built-in Tailwind utilities** (`flex`, `text-sm`, `font-semibold`, `rounded-md`, …).

3. **To compose custom styles:**
   - Expand utilities inline in `@apply`, or
   - Apply the component class in TSX/HTML (`className="app-text-p1-regular text-average"`), or
   - Use plain CSS properties instead of `@apply` for that part.

4. **Figma / design alignment workflow:**
   - Layout and spacing in CSS: `@apply flex gap-6 rounded-md …` (built-in only).
   - Typography + semantic color: **in TSX** or raw CSS properties (`font-family`, `color: var(--average-text-color)`).
   - After editing `artifacts/aprly/src/styles/**/*.css`, run `check:tailwind-apply`.

5. **After editing any `*.css` with `@apply`**, run:
   ```bash
   pnpm --filter @workspace/aprly run check:tailwind-apply
   ```

## Examples from this repo

| Custom class | Where to use |
|---|---|
| `dash-text-sm-sb` | TSX, or expand to `text-sm font-semibold` in `@apply` |
| `app-text-p1-regular` | TSX `className`, or `font-family`/`font-size`/`font-weight` in CSS |
| `text-average` | TSX `className`, or `color: var(--average-text-color)` in CSS |
| `app-button-button-l-m` | TSX only |
